    "body": "Owner questions, 9 October 2026.\n\n**How the next token is predicted** (`docs/geometry.md`, new `next-token.svg` generated by `generate.py`, README link):\n- The seven code-confirmed steps of the geometric stack: embedding, the quaternion recurrence, Lorentz/Dot reads, SwiGLU, the tied logits head, and the copy head with prime routing. Then D11 serving.\n- A \"What it does not use\" note: no Hamming distances, spin or spherical harmonics in the stack's prediction path.\n- A **Softmax at runtime** table:\n  - the served next-token choice is a greedy argmax over integer scores, with no softmax;\n  - read-layer weights are still a table-emulated softmax (sealed exp table plus integer normalization);\n  - the flock rank tables are the softmax-free path that already exists;\n  - the copy-head mixture is fixed point.\n\n**VSA re-review** (cadence record):\n- `docs/labs/vsa-review-2026-10-09/README.md`: an independent review of DeepSeek's 8 October VSA measurements. Two are valid but aren't VSA tests; the two codebook tests are inconclusive because they used a frozen artifact with no retraining.\n- A newest-first `current-state.md` entry that re-scopes \"inert\" and pre-registers a retraining test (4 arms × 2 seeds, KEEP at ≥ 0.01 BPB, retire below 0.005).\n\nChecks: claim wording passes; `generate.py` is deterministic; the new SVG parses with no external references and was rendered and inspected.\n\nReferences #2029 #2032\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
